1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,940
He sold a fake masterpiece to a Nazi leader.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:06,260
Now meet Han van Meegeren, a Dutch painter.

3
00:00:06,780 --> 00:00:10,340
His trick was faking Johannes Vermeer, a Dutch master from the sixteen hundreds.

4
00:00:11,800 --> 00:00:15,180
Real Vermeers are rare, so a new one is like buried treasure.

5
00:00:15,760 --> 00:00:18,600
So he painted new ones himself, in Vermeer's style.

6
00:00:19,180 --> 00:00:22,320
Then he sold them as lost paintings that were just discovered.

7
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,900
And the art experts actually bought it.

8
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:26,760
Hit like if you'd have been fooled too.

9
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:31,260
In nineteen forty-three, one fake went to Hermann Goering, a Nazi leader.

10
00:00:31,660 --> 00:00:35,920
He paid one point six five million guilders. That was Dutch money back then.

11
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:40,040
Two years later, after the war, investigators found it in Goering's collection.

12
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:43,580
Then they traced it back to van Meegeren, and he was arrested.

13
00:00:44,040 --> 00:00:47,020
The charge was collaboration, which means helping the enemy.

14
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:50,520
So how do you get out of that? You confess to something smaller.

15
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,340
Here's what he said: I didn't sell a treasure. I painted it myself.

16
00:00:54,820 --> 00:00:57,880
Send this to the friend who always has one wild excuse.

17
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:01,920
Still, nobody believed him, so he asked for paint and a canvas.

18
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:06,260
Then, while officials watched, he painted a brand-new fake Vermeer.

19
00:01:06,660 --> 00:01:08,900
Now he wasn't a traitor anymore, just a faker.

20
00:01:09,460 --> 00:01:12,200
Follow if you love when the confession is the escape plan.

21
00:01:12,740 --> 00:01:15,740
Then the charge changed to forgery, which means faking art.

22
00:01:16,180 --> 00:01:19,180
In nineteen forty-seven, he was sentenced to one year in prison.

23
00:01:19,740 --> 00:01:22,460
Weeks later, he died, before he ever served it.

24
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:26,020
So the fake that could have ruined him actually saved him.

25
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,460
Genius or crook? One word.

